  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangents on the ellipse <math><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> are perpendicular to each other, then <math><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to"
  },
